From dd2c5624587cf5c1a433af38cb022836a7b30a09 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Bjoern Bachmann <bjoern.bachmann@ni.com>
Date: Tue, 28 Apr 2026 13:48:25 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 10/13] mpm: refactor thermal/fan sensor handling with unified
 hwmon/sysfs abstraction

Introduce HwmonTempSensors (sysfs_hwmon.py) and refactor
SysfsThermalSensors (sysfs_thermal.py) to enumerate available sensors
once at construction time and cache device references in a sensor_map
dict, avoiding repeated udev context creation and device-tree walks on
every readout.

HwmonTempSensors supports the cros-ec hwmon subsystem and accepts a
sensor_list parameter to discover both temp and fan sensors. A new
read_fan_sensor_value() method is added alongside the existing
read_thermal_sensor_value(). Multiple subsystems (hwmon, iio) and
sensor formats are supported via a read_sysfs_sensors_value() utility.

SysfsThermalSensors is extended to support multiple subsystems (IIO
and thermal) and a data_probe parameter for flexible attribute reading.
A read_fan_sensor_value() method is added to match the hwmon interface.

Both classes expose the same read_thermal_sensor_value(sensor_names,
reduce_fn) interface, making them interchangeable at the call site.

All affected peripheral managers are updated:
- E320: updated to use the new sensor abstraction pattern
- N3xx: refactored temp and fan sensor methods for hwmon/thermal backends
- X4xx: unified _temp_fan_sensors handle with hwmon/thermal dispatch,
  add missing HwmonTempSensors import
- E310: add dynamic MB temperature sensor type detection instead of
  hardcoding "jc-42.4-temp", fixing usrp_list_sensors compatibility

A _hwmon_based_sensors flag at init time selects the correct backend
for fan and temperature reads on all platforms.
